comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-02T22:10:16.764Z",codex-sol,"Restart by codex-sol: preserved remote PR #118 and all existing bot replies/reactions were inspected. Branch is already current with origin/main. No new actionable unresolved inline finding is present. Retain documented coverage/health/publication blockers; rerun unchanged full CI gate with the host-wide flock. No merge, publish or item closure."
  "2026-10-02T22:25:27.456Z",codex-sol,"Restart: locked npm ci and release:check pass 196/196 tests, zero skips, configured 100% lines/branches/functions over three sources, without a separate statements dimension. The PM-linked seven-test real prepare-launcher suite passes both malformed package states. Strict health with merge drivers and tracked build output equality pass. The prior run-callback migration fix and f4dea28 broken-install regressions remain unchanged. Whole-source coverage pm-starter-puy5, existing public-history/publication privacy blocker pm-starter-asud, and substantive final-head reviews remain open. No merge, publish or close; release claim for orchestrator."
notes[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-29T14:50:00.484Z",codex,"2026-09-29 baseline on main head 27941da: direct npm run release:check passed with installed CLI SDK, pm-ops and pm-changelog 2026.9.23, zero production audit findings and changelog parity. npm registry now publishes CLI SDK and pm-ops 2026.9.29 and pm-changelog 2026.9.25. Candidate exact-pins those three in package and lockfile; scripts/prepare-merge-driver.ts is copied byte-for-byte from the published pm-ops 2026.9.29 template and npm run prepare passed. Current CLI binary reports 2026.9.29. Full new-pin gate, packed npm/Bun behavior and remote review still pending. Existing privacy issue pm-starter-asud and release-auth/order issues remain independent blockers."
  "2026-09-29T15:02:07.460Z",codex,"2026-09-29 red-green packed acceptance: the original packed candidate on published CLI 2026.9.29 installed and ran starter greet/summary in a real npm project, but strict health failed extension_migration_pending for pm-starter-0001-noop; pm package migrate returned ok=true with pending_count=1 and no receipt. Inspecting published SDK types showed SchemaMigrationDefinition.run is the executable hook; package source incorrectly used up. A focused test expecting run failed with TypeError, then passed after changing the callback to run. Repacked candidate SHA-256 03dc3688497cdb88ed007fbaafed414191dc3b8c68754ed31fa284e6460ac45e. Fresh npm/npx and Bun/bunx projects on CLI 2026.9.29 installed it, created one real task, invoked starter greet and summary, auto-applied the demo migration, and passed strict PM health with zero warnings. Explicit package migrate then reported skipped_count=1 with before=applied in each project. Direct and PM-linked npm run release:check passed 195/195 tests, zero skips, 6 docstring files/32 declarations, configured 100% lines/branches/functions across 3 sources, zero production audit, pack/changelog/attestation. Statement coverage and three authored executable scripts are outside that claim under pm-starter-puy5. Public-history privacy and release-auth/order issues remain open; no publication or merge approval is claimed."
  "2026-09-29T15:12:34.607Z",codex,"Greptile P2 on PR #118 at head d4d62e0 found missing launcher fixtures for a dangling pm-ops link and a directory lacking package.json. Added both real child-process checkout cases to the existing test and confirmed 7/7 focused tests pass, with nonzero failure and no registered drivers for either broken state. Full release gate is running before the review-fix push."
  "2026-09-29T15:13:12.727Z",codex,"Review-fix precommit full release gate passed: 196/196 tests, zero skips, configured three-source coverage thresholds, zero production audit findings, pack/changelog/attestation. Greptile inline P2 was positively reacted to and answered with exact fixture assertions. This does not close the all-source coverage or historical privacy blockers."
